+// KenshiLib ships only a forward declaration, but the 'crafting' member below is
+// a std::deque<CraftingItem> BY VALUE, and the VC10 STL instantiates deque on the
+// member declaration - which needs a complete type. Give it an opaque definition.
+// This cannot move any member offset: MSVC's deque stores a map pointer plus three
+// size_t and never embeds T, so sizeof(deque<T>) is identical for every T (the
+// mirrored layout here has it spanning 0x498..0x4C8 either way). Nothing reads the
+// deque's elements; it exists so the offsets of the members after it stay right.
+class CraftingItem {};
 
